      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/28/trump-xi-jinping-china-buy-weapons",
      "description": "<p>David Perdue’s remarks come after a Taiwanese minister spoke of the ‘severe’ military threat posed by Beijing to the self-ruled island</p><p>Donald Trump offered to sell weapons to China while hosting its leader, Xi Jinping, last week, the US ambassador to China said on Sunday.</p><p>David Perdue told Fox News on Sunday: “President Trump continues to say, hey, we sell arms to other people around the world. He actually asked President Xi, would he like to buy some at one point.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/28/trump-xi-jinping-china-buy-weapons\">Continue reading...</a>",
